      "role": "user",
      "content": "ugh help... im literally in the middle of this town hall and things are going south fast. one of the local shop owners just stood up and basically said the gov is intentionally picking winners and losers, and that these new environmental regs are basically a death sentence for our town while big lobbyists in dc get all the perks. he's making a huge scene and saying we're basically being betrayed. i need some hard-hitting points to help the rep defend us... like how can we frame this not just as a 'cost of doing business' but as an actual targeted attack on our local way of life and small towns?",
